data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":769,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_016e32f97ebf3c7e016aca0ed2b9bc8194bb646b993c8a7eb6","call_id":"call_459dcbfc9919470e82919aade9fe4e89","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"  due_date TEXT\\n);`);\",\"newText\":\"  due_date TEXT,\\n  position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\\n);`);\"},{\"oldText\":\"try { db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN due_date TEXT'); } catch (error) { if (!String(error.message).includes('duplicate column')) throw error; }\",\"newText\":\"try { db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN due_date TEXT'); } catch (error) { if (!String(error.message).includes('duplicate column')) throw error; }\\ntry { db.exec('ALTER TABLE tasks ADD COLUMN position INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0'); } catch (error) { if (!String(error.message).includes('duplicate column')) throw error; }\\ndb.exec('UPDATE tasks SET position = id WHERE position = 0');\"},{\"oldText\":\"  const taskRoute = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/tasks(?:\\\\/(\\\\d+))?$/);\",\"newText\":\"  const moveRoute = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/tasks\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/move$/);\\n  if (moveRoute && req.method === 'POST') {\\n    const sourceId = Number(moveRoute[1]);\\n    const taskId = Number(moveRoute[2]);\\n    const source = db.prepare('SELECT archived FROM projects WHERE id = ?').get(sourceId);\\n    if (!source) return send(res, 404, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Project not found' }));\\n    if (source.archived) return send(res, 403, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Project is archived' }));\\n    const body = await requestBody(req);\\n    const destinationId = Number(body?.destination_id);\\n    const destination = db.prepare('SELECT archived FROM projects WHERE id = ?').get(destinationId);\\n    if (!destination || destination.archived || destinationId === sourceId) return send(res, 400, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid destination' }));\\n    const task = db.prepare('SELECT id FROM tasks WHERE id = ? AND project_id = ?').get(taskId, sourceId);\\n    if (!task) return send(res, 404, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Task not found' }));\\n    const position = db.prepare('SELECT COALESCE(MAX(position), 0) + 1 AS next FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ?').get(destinationId).next;\\n    db.prepare('UPDATE tasks SET project_id = ?, position = ? WHERE id = ?').run(destinationId, position, taskId);\\n    return send(res, 200, JSON.stringify({ ok: true }));\\n  }\\n  const taskRoute = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/(\\\\d+)\\\\/tasks(?:\\\\/(\\\\d+))?$/);\"},{\"oldText\":\"SELECT id, title, completed, priority, due_date FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ? ORDER BY id\",\"newText\":\"SELECT id, title, completed, priority, due_date FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ? ORDER BY position, id\"},{\"oldText\":\"INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority) VALUES (?, ?, ?)\",\"newText\":\"INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority, position) VALUES (?, ?, ?, (SELECT COALESCE(MAX(position), 0) + 1 FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ?))\"},{\"oldText\":\".run(projectId, title, project.default_priority);\",\"newText\":\".run(projectId, title, project.default_priority, projectId);\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":770,"response":{"id":"resp_016e32f97ebf3c7e016aca0ece30d881949b8ea58530b2a94c","object":"response","created_at":1791626958,"completed_at":1791626964,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6-luna","access_programs":null,"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\